@startuml j2-safety-replies
!include style.iuml
title J2 Safety replies
actor Patient
participant "Patient chat\n(index.html, chat.js,\nsync.js, shared.js)" as Chat
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core
database "Browser storage" as LS
participant "api/messages.js" as Msg
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix
database "Store (Postgres)\nthrough api/_store.js" as Store
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : types the message and presses Send
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(message, clinic file, language)
Core -> Core : checks in order: emergency, a rule change round a symptom,\nrule change or discount, medical; "not sure" when the file has no answer
alt emergency
  Core --> Chat : the emergency reply, status "urgent"
else rule change or discount
  Core --> Chat : the refusal, status "answered"
else medical
  Core --> Chat : the medical reply, status "needs human"
else not sure
  Core --> Chat : the not-sure reply, status "needs human"
end
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question, reply, status)
Core -> LS : the ticket joins this browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : the fixed reply; api/chat.js is not called
Chat -> Msg : shared.js: POST /api/messages (the question, then the reply)
Msg -> Store : rows in the table messages
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets (the ticket, with this browser's key)
Tix -> Store : a row in the table tickets; priority "urgent" for an emergency
@enduml
